Hello,

in the following code, Spec# complains that &quot;A.a&quot; is inaccesible du to its protection level. I can get rid of this error message by declaring &quot;a&quot; public. I feel that a contract of a method should have acces to a private member. What is wrong?

using System;

using Microsoft.Contracts;




class A 

{

	int a;

	invariant 0 &lt;= a;




	public void foo(int k)

	requires 0 &lt;= k &lt;= a;

	{

		a -= k;

	}



}

Regards,
Boris
